      "id": 1,
      "text": "Farmersville Station, built in 1890, housed a church, hotel, hardware store, three general stores, a blacksmith, a mill, a cheese factory, a telegraph office, and a post office.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://historicpath.org/history/farmersville",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Buffalo, Rochester & Pittsburgh railroad cut through Farmersville’s northern border in 1878, establishing a vital rail link for the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.city-data.com/city/Farmersville-Pennsylvania.html",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1880s, Farmersville Center boasted two churches, a schoolhouse, a hotel, a general store, two blacksmiths, two shoe shops, a wagon shop, a harness shop, a grist mill, and a cheese factory run by the Howden Brothers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://historicpath.org/history/farmersville",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first permanent settlement in Farmersville began at the site of the current station in 1817, long before the town’s formal founding.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://historicpath.org/history/farmersville",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Every Tuesday, Farmersville hosts a lively weekly auction that draws locals and visitors alike.",
